{
  "_readme": [
    "LEVEL DATA FOR THE LAST GAME.",
    "You can edit this file in any text editor - no Godot needed.",
    "",
    "GRID SYMBOLS:",
    "  #  wall        .  floor",
    "  P  player start (exactly one per level)",
    "  G  goal         O  pit (fall in and you die - jump over it)",
    "  C  checkpoint coin (OPTIONAL, at most one per level)",
    "",
    "THE CHECKPOINT COIN (C):",
    "  Only does anything on STANDARD difficulty. Pick it up and this",
    "  level becomes your fallback: lose all 3 lives later and you",
    "  restart HERE with a fresh 3 lives instead of going back to 1.",
    "  Placed on levels 10, 20 and 30, each time behind something",
    "  dangerous so taking it is a real decision, not a freebie.",
    "",
    "HAZARD TYPES (positions are [column, row], counting from 0):",
    "  patrol  - moves a to b. LOW, so you CAN jump over it.",
    "  sweep   - same as patrol but fast. LOW, you MUST jump it.",
    "  chain   - spins around pivot. TALL, you CANNOT jump it. Go around.",
    "            'arms' puts 2+ orbs on one pivot, evenly spaced.",
    "  chaser  - follows the player, forever. LOW.",
    "  blinker - sits still and pulses on/off. Only kills while lit.",
    "            'period' = seconds per cycle, 'duty' = share of the cycle",
    "            it is lethal, 'phase' = 0..1 offset so several blinkers",
    "            alternate with each other.",
    "",
    "'speed' is a multiplier - bigger is faster.",
    "",
    "DIFFICULTY CURVE: 1-5 teach, 6-9 build, 10 checkpoint,",
    "11-19 introduce chaser/blinker/twin-arm chains, 20 checkpoint,",
    "21-29 combinations at speed, 30 is the finale."
  ],
